OL,3,GNEWSAThe town that was once the
OL,4,Aepicentre of basketball in England
OL,5,
OL,6,FA town better known for its historic
OL,7,Fshipbuilding and industry may seem an
OL,8,Funlikely place to be the birthplace of
OL,9,Fbasketball in England, but in 1892
OL,10,FBirkenhead became the epicentre of the
OL,11,Fsport.
OL,13,FIt was during a business trip to Canada
OL,14,Fthat the president of the town's YMCA,
OL,15,FC J Proctor, first came across the game
OL,16,Fand introduced the sport at
OL,17,FBirkenhead's YMCA gym on Merseyside
OL,18,Fwhen he returned.
OL,20,FInvented just a year earlier, the game
OL,21,Finvolved bouncing a ball into a fruit
OL,22,Fbasket on a 10-foot-tall (3.05m) pole.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
